# Citation metadata for the Security Data Works systematic literature review.
# A Zenodo DOI is minted on the first tagged GitHub release (owner-held step;
# see docs/ZENODO-RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md). Once minted, the concept DOI is added
# under `identifiers:` below and becomes the citation target.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this literature review, please cite the Zenodo DOI once it is
  minted on the first tagged release (it will be recorded in this file under
  identifiers, and the release checklist in docs/ replaces the manuscript's
  DOI placeholders at the same time); until then, please cite the title and
  repository URL below.
type: dataset
title: "Modern Data Architecture for Cybersecurity Operations: A Systematic Literature Review"
authors:
  - family-names: Wiley
    given-names: Jeremy
    affiliation: Security Data Works
repository-code: "https://github.com/flying-coyote/security-data-literature-review"
abstract: >-
  Security organizations evaluating modern data stack architectures (Apache
  Iceberg, ClickHouse, Kafka Streams) face fragmented literature: cybersecurity
  research focuses on detection algorithms while data engineering addresses
  general analytics, leaving security-specific infrastructure guidance
  unavailable. We conduct the first systematic literature review bridging these
  domains using PRISMA-aligned methodology, synthesizing 75+ sources spanning
  production deployments, peer-reviewed research, and government standards to
  provide operational guidance.
keywords:
  - data lakehouse
  - security analytics
  - OLAP
  - streaming architectures
  - cybersecurity data engineering
  - systematic literature review
